From 43f36c9d58c6be4e86e020b3233592ffc9626d94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:59:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] Stereoscopics: settle the display mode for a 3D source
 in one change

Starting a stereoscopic title reconfigured the display three times in the six seconds
before the film appeared, and on a projector each of those is a resynchronisation - the
last of them, into a 3D mode, several seconds of it.

The first came from the search that runs when the video stream opens. The stereo mode
that decides what the display mode has to carry is applied when the first picture
reaches the renderer, which on a 4K file is seconds later, so the search ran while the
output was still 2D and picked the 2D mode of the right timing - a mode chosen for a
frame nobody was going to see, since nothing of the film is on screen until the picture
that settles the question arrives. Leave the display alone until then. Only where a
stereo mode is certain to be applied without asking: with the playback mode set to ask
the viewer's answer may be a while coming, and with it set to ignore no mode is coming
at all, so in both the search goes ahead as before.

The second and third were the stereo mode and the display mode arriving separately.
Applying a stereo mode re-applies the display mode by itself - the surface changes shape
with it - so the mode change that follows a moment later, when the player's search has
run, reconfigures a display that was reconfigured for the same reason a frame earlier.
Choose that mode when the stereo mode is applied and hand the two over together, which
is what CGraphicContext::SetStereoMode() now takes. The player is still asked to run its
search: that is what keeps the display latency and its own parameters in step, and by
then the mode is already set, so it settles on the same one and changes nothing.

ChooseBestResolution() therefore has to be able to choose for an arrangement that has
not been applied yet, so it takes the one to choose for, defaulting to the arrangement
the graphics context has been given. Writing the resolution before the mode keeps a flip
from seeing one without the other.

Which mode a stereoscopic source's search is waiting for is the manager's to say, so it
says it - IsStereoModeSettled(), true once it has decided for a stereoscopic stream. The
decision is announced as a stream change like any other, so where it changed nothing the
search that was deferred still has to be asked for; that ask is made once, since
servicing it is announced as a stream change in turn and asking again on that would not
end.

Finally, compare the mode in effect against the arrangement the display can carry rather
than the one the source asks for. They differ whenever the display carries only the
other arrangement, and a source left in its own - which is what happens when the
geometry needed to choose is not known yet - would otherwise never be revisited.

(cherry picked from commit 479504782bfcd93408aadf209c9fffdec1475503)
